raphael: connect the iOS brightness slider to DCS 0x51 (IOMFB selector 50 + backlight service)

Two paths reach the panel, and both were missing:

1. iOS 18's brightness stack only drives a display it can bind a brightness
   control to. The service added in 0243/0249 published backlight-control and
   IODisplayParameters.brightness, which made backboardd find it -- and then
   crash inside CoreBrightness-+0x14659c, in CoreFoundation, with a NULL
   object (reproduced on the phone: sig 11 code 0xb, far 0). A disassembly of
   that address shows IORegistryEntryCreateCFProperty -> CFDictionaryGetValue
   (dict, key) -> CFNumberGetValue(value, kCFNumberFloatType) -> /65536.0: a
   calibration lookup returns NULL. UniXNU-pclm10's record says CoreBrightness
   requires all nine backlight-calibration-parameters keys (including
   current-for-max/mid-backlight and hardware-max-current-limit) before it
   starts the libEDR server and delivers brightness-nits. This patch publishes
   exactly the set a working AppleARMBacklight publishes (Trogdor-ipadOS
   CoachzBacklight.cpp: the six l*Product/l*Panel luminances as 16.16 nits,
   current-for-*-backlight and hardware-max-current-limit as 0, plus
   milliAmps2NitsScaleFactor), the marketing table and
   new-backlight-architecture, IODisplayParameters.brightness/BrightnessMilliNits
   (2/140/500 nits), takes both request forms (brightness 0..2047 and
   brightness-nits signed 16.16), and turns the service on by default for
   raphael -- without it the slider is frozen. A level becomes one DCS 0x51
   packet through raphael_dsi.c (sweetfb_blsvc=0 turns the service off,
   raphael_dcs=0 the DCS path). Every property read is logged (0286) while the
   service is being brought up.

2. The iOS 18 USB log shows backboardd calling IOMobileFramebuffer selector
   50 (setBrightnessCorrection) with 0..10000 units. externalMethod had no
   case for it, so those requests were dropped; the case maps them onto the
   same DCS levels with a perceptual table (the low third of the slider needs
   the small levels), as ios-raphael patch 0100 does.

